vectors.json: ground truth for muster's LEZ v0.3.0 public-transaction encoder (lez/tx.nim).

It was generated by generator/, a Rust program built against LEZ's own crates: lee,
lee_core and common from logos-blockchain/logos-execution-zone @ v0.3.0, the line the
public testnet runs since 2026-09-30 (exo-eb6.4).

Regenerate it with the generator's Cargo.lock (committed). The build needs the same
system libraries as the LEZ sequencer (infra/lez/localnet.sh's header: a C++ compiler,
libclang); a binary built with nixpkgs#gcc also needs nix's libstdc++ to run:

  cd generator && RISC0_SKIP_BUILD=1 cargo +1.98.1 build -q
  LD_LIBRARY_PATH=<nixpkgs#gcc.cc^lib>/lib target/debug/lez-vectors-v030 > ../vectors.json

Generated 2026-10-01.

What it pins:
- keys: account id = SHA-256("/LEE/v0.3/AccountId/Public/" padded ‖ BIP-340 x-only key),
  unchanged from v0.2.4.
- txs: native transfers (program account 0, the reserved native token program; both
  rows select the native shard; the instruction is borsh Transfer { amount: u128 }):
  - Message borsh and Message::hash ("/LEE/v0.3/Message/Public/" padded ‖ borsh), with
    the shard selectors, u128 nonces, the instruction bytes, and Option<FeeDeclaration>
    { payer, gas_limit u64, tip u64, max_fee u128 };
  - self-pay, a co-signing payer (its signature and nonce after the others), and the
    fee-exempt None tag;
  - BIP-340 signatures, PublicTransaction borsh + hash, and LeeTransaction::Public borsh in
    base64 (what sendTransaction takes). WitnessSet::is_valid_for and is_fee_authorized
    are asserted before output; signatures use 32 zero bytes of aux randomness.
- the LEZ wallet's fee defaults: gas_limit 2_000_000, max_fee (2_000_000 + 100_000) × 64 =
  134_400_000, the values its CLI sent on the local v0.3 zone.
